# NEXT FOR THE PAPER (prepared 2026-10-06, smoke run first; user, 2026-10-04): Kimi-Dev-72B (Moonshot AI, MIT license), a coding model fine-tuned from Qwen2.5-72B.
# One A100/H100 80GB at 4 bits (~40 GB). Checked on Hugging Face, 2026-10-04:
#   - No published EAGLE-3 head for Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct or Kimi-Dev-72B.
#   - Closest compatible EAGLE-3 head: AQ-MedAI/Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct-eagle3 (MIT; same shapes as Kimi-Dev-72B:
#     hidden size 8192, vocabulary 152,064). It was trained for the vision-language model, whose language part is
#     Qwen2.5-72B-based, so it is a warm start, not a fit; few downloads, quality unknown. We refit it to
#     Kimi-Dev-72B's own answers. Report it as "closest published head", not as Kimi-Dev's published head.
#   - Not usable as a start: yuhuili/EAGLE-Qwen2-72B-Instruct (older EAGLE format, Qwen2-72B); jeqcho/qwen-2.5-72b-
#     instruct-eagle-ft* (LoRA adapters, not draft heads).
#   - 4-bit files for SGLang: QuantTrio/Kimi-Dev-72B-GPTQ-Int4 (served by Marlin kernels, like our Qwen3-30B-A3B),
#     or AWQ: abhishekchohan/Kimi-Dev-72B-AWQ, cyankiwi/Kimi-Dev-72B-AWQ-4bit (compressed-tensors format).
#   - Ollama: no official tag; import a GGUF (bartowski/moonshotai_Kimi-Dev-72B-GGUF or unsloth/Kimi-Dev-72B-GGUF,
#     Q4_K_M) with a Modelfile and record its sha256 (modelinfo/).
#   - Coding model: training answers should come from coding prompts (e.g. a code-instruction set), not Dolly; time
#     HumanEval-style prompts; outputs are long. Also worth running: the same head trained from scratch, to measure
#     what the warm start is worth (needs the from-scratch option in run_model.sh).
MODEL=kimi-dev-72b
TARGET=QuantTrio/Kimi-Dev-72B-GPTQ-Int4               # verify it serves in SGLang (smoke run)
PUB_HEAD=AQ-MedAI/Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct-eagle3      # closest published head (warm start only)
OLLAMA_TAG=kimi-dev:72b                               # created locally from the imported GGUF
OLLAMA_GGUF=mradermacher/Kimi-Dev-72B-GGUF:Kimi-Dev-72B.Q4_K_M.gguf   # 47.4 GB, single file (bartowski/unsloth have no Q4_K_M)
OLLAMA_TEMPLATE=qwen2.5                               # modelfiles/qwen2.5.modelfile: Kimi-Dev uses Qwen2.5's chat template
TRAIN_SOURCE=mix                                      # half Magicoder coding tasks (MIT, decontaminated), half Dolly
SF_TEMPLATE=qwen
CHAT_KWARGS='{}'
SYSTEM_TURN=0
CTX=4096

# Pinned: the exact files behind the published results (from precomputed/kimi-dev-72b/CHECKSUMS.json). The pipeline downloads
# these revisions, refuses an Ollama file with another sha256, and RETEST=1 uses HEAD_SHA256 from files.sushila.ai.
TARGET_REV=57a4cb1a3012968e5e2f3772a9877879be1a8f9a
PUB_HEAD_REV=bdd66af1bb4aafba09f5e5c7f975e3f1ff86ed57
OLLAMA_SHA256=67b8610bb120fe10256fb2cf94b2a50d590826c46ad18821a22bf083c5b46fa8
HEAD_SHA256=b83864872c3d5bc558af898635f1b4bb926ff94213cba104c507e3a99a1dd7e7
HEAD_CONFIG_SHA256=302c4048e48bba75f5ec3fd6fc885dac692b108fbe485da983c644d0e52f6c2d
OLLAMA_GGUF_REV=a1c3c37eb57c84de93e381860272ab0c63391d8f   # file unchanged since 5f31397 (sha256 = OLLAMA_SHA256)
